{"agentId":"a00714bb97a5fae10","cwd":"/home/user/HeadacheRecording","entrypoint":"remote","gitBranch":"claude/determined-keller-1oTSo","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":"Build a complete headache and medication recording web app in /home/user/HeadacheRecording. The app should be a single-page React app (using Vite + React + TypeScript).\n\n## Features Required\n\n1. **Record headache severity** for a given date:\n   - 首痛止まり (neck pain only)\n   - 頭痛（仕事できる）(headache, can work)\n   - 頭痛（ギリ仕事できる）(headache, barely can work)\n   - 頭痛（仕事できない）(headache, cannot work)\n\n2. **Record medication intake** (頓服薬) with time:\n   - ドンペリドン (Domperidone)\n   - ナラトリプタン (Naratriptan)\n   - Multiple medications can be recorded per day\n\n3. **Monthly calendar view** showing each day's headache level color-coded:\n   - No entry: white/gray\n   - 首痛止まり: light yellow\n   - 頭痛（仕事できる）: orange\n   - 頭痛（ギリ仕事できる）: light red\n   - 頭痛（仕事できない）: red\n\n4. **PDF export** of monthly summary showing:\n   - Calendar with colors\n   - List of medication days and counts\n   - Monthly statistics (headache days per severity, medication usage count)\n\n## Technical Stack\n- Vite + React + TypeScript\n- Use `localStorage` for data persistence\n- Use `jsPDF` + `html2canvas` for PDF generation (install via npm)\n- Tailwind CSS for styling (install via npm)\n- Japanese UI throughout\n\n## Implementation Steps\n\n1. Run: `cd /home/user/HeadacheRecording && npm create vite@latest . -- --template react-ts` (answer yes to any prompts)\n2. Install dependencies: `npm install && npm install jspdf html2canvas && npm install -D tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite`\n3. Configure Tailwind in vite.config.ts and create CSS\n4. Build the full app with these components:\n   - `App.tsx` - main layout with month navigation\n   - `CalendarView.tsx` - monthly calendar grid\n   - `DayModal.tsx` - modal to add/edit headache and medication for a day\n   - `MonthlyStats.tsx` - summary statistics panel\n   - `PDFExport.tsx` - PDF generation function\n   - `types.ts` - TypeScript types\n   - `storage.ts` - localStorage read/write helpers\n\n## Data Model (store in localStorage as JSON)\n```typescript\ntype HeadacheLevel = 'neck' | 'mild' | 'moderate' | 'severe';\ntype Medication = { name: string; time: string };\ntype DayRecord = {\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\n  headacheLevel?: HeadacheLevel;\n  medications: Medication[];\n  notes?: string;\n};\n```\n\n## Key UI Details\n- Header with month navigation (prev/next arrows) and current month display\n- Calendar grid (Sun-Sat) with colored day cells\n- Click a day cell to open modal for that day\n- Modal has: severity radio buttons, medication add section (select med + time input + add button), notes textarea, save/delete buttons\n- Below calendar: stats table showing count per severity and medication totals\n- \"PDF出力\" button to generate and download PDF\n\nPlease implement the complete working app. Run `npm run build` at the end to verify it compiles. Write all files needed.\n\nIMPORTANT: The working directory is /home/user/HeadacheRecording. The branch to commit to is `claude/determined-keller-1oTSo`. After building successfully, commit and push all files.\n","role":"user"},"parentUuid":null,"promptId":"d0deaa64-e137-4776-8064-866c1c509187","sessionId":"049d03a0-a4cb-507f-a2bf-0f606bd0e31c","timestamp":"2026-06-06T05:30:41.026Z","type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"cc72834a-66ae-4423-82a6-a994a408c949","version":"2.1.167"}
